.TH WB\-ACCEPT 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-accept \- accept the file of an issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR accept <issue> [\-\-no\-commit | \-n] [\-q | \-\-quiet]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Accept the work of an issue. The issue's file .watchbill/issues/<issue>.yml is accepted by wb plan accept, which does this: read it, hold it to its form, refuse it while it holds a question, say what will be written, and write .watchbill/issues/<issue>.accepted with the SHA\-256 of the file, the git user.name and user.email, and the time in UTC. An acceptance that is there is never written over. Then commit it alone, on the issue's branch, with nothing else: it refuses first when the checkout is not on that branch or the issue's file is not committed as it is.
.PP
\-\-no\-commit (\-n) only writes it and says the commit. Where the issue's file is not accepted, a plan or not, wb accept ends with 2 and names wb plan accept <name>. Where it is accepted as it stands, it accepts the work: it says first accepting the work <commit> (not run: <roles>), then writes .watchbill/issues/<issue>.finished with the head commit of the branch, who and when, and commits it alone. It ends with 1 when no role has committed work, a question is open, a view is kept with work not taken back, or the change touches classed code, which needs a person as verifier. A later commit on the branch voids it. The job is then done. Ends with 0 when it is accepted, 1 when it is refused, 2 when it was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.PP
wb plan accept and wb accept also make a tag signed with the person's SSH key (git tag \-s): refs/tags/watchbill/accept/<name>/<12 hex digits> on the blob of the issue's file, and refs/tags/watchbill/finished/<name>/<12 hex digits> on the commit the record names, the digits being the first of the SHA\-256 of the .accepted or .finished. Each refuses with 1 before it writes anything where git has no user.signingkey or gpg.format is not ssh, and where the tag it made does not check against the keys of .watchbill/signers with the role accept, which it then removes. An acceptance whose tag is not there, unsigned, or signed by a key not in the list or without accept counts for nothing. wb pushes nothing, and says the command that pushes the tag. After a signed acceptance it committed, wb plan accept posts an [accepted] notice by issue_comment, which wb never reads back. A missing list is refused, never skipped: where the default branch holds no .watchbill/signers or one with no key line, or there is no default branch, nothing is signed and no acceptance counts, and wb plan accept and wb accept end with 1 before they write anything, naming the file and how to add a key to it.
.PP
\-q (\-\-quiet) leaves out the check of the lists and the lines that confirm the write and the commit, and not what it will write or commit, the command to commit or push, or a refusal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commit, \-n
Only write the acceptance and say the commit.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Leave out the lines that only confirm what was done or say there was nothing to do; never a refusal, a warning, what is said before a write, or a command the person has to run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is accepted.
.TP
.B 1
It is refused: no file, a fault of form, a question, an acceptance that is there, no git identity, a path of changes under build_files, a list that leaves out what a file needs to build, no .watchbill/signers on the default branch or one with no key line, no signing key, or a tag that does not check.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly (no issue, a word that is not known, a name that is not an issue), a plan of the name is there and is not accepted (wb plan accept <name> accepts it), the folder is not in a git repository, or Watchbill is not set up.
